kov-kernel argument of `stationaryEnv` is given inline rather than through the instance\nabove: the nested proof of an exposed `def` becomes a public auxiliary constant, whereas the proof\ninside an instance (a theorem) becomes a module-private one, which the standalone comparator\nchallenges (`comparator/`) could not reproduce. ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"E","role":"type","type":"Type u_1","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"NormedAddCommGroup","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"NormedAddCommGroup E","typeRefs":[[0,18,"NormedAddCommGroup"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"InnerProductSpace","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"InnerProductSpace ℝ E","typeRefs":[[0,17,"InnerProductSpace"],[18,19,"Real"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace E","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"OpensMeasurableSpace","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"OpensMeasurableSpace E","typeRefs":[[0,20,"OpensMeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"Set","implicit":false,"name":"𝒳","role":"variable","type":"Set E","typeRefs":[[0,3,"Set"]]},{"explicit":true,"implicit":false,"name":"θ","role":"variable","type":"E","typeRefs":[]}],"conclusion":"Environment Unit ↑𝒳 ℝ","conclusionHead":"Learning.Environment","conclusionRefs":[[0,11,"Learning.Environment"],[12,16,"Unit"],[20,21,"Real"]],"decl":"Learning.LinearBandit.linearGaussianEnv","value":"stationaryEnv (linearGaussianKernel 𝒳 θ)","valueRefs":[[0,13,"Learning.stationaryEnv"],[15,35,"Learning.LinearBandit.linearGaussianKernel"]]},"code":"/-- The linear Gaussian environment on the action set `𝒳` with reward vector `θ`: the stationary\nenvironment with reward kernel `linearGaussianKernel 𝒳 θ`.\n\nThe Markov-kernel argument of `stationaryEnv` is given inline rather than through the instance\nabove: the nested proof of an exposed `def` becomes a public auxiliary constant, whereas the proof\ninside an instance (a theorem) becomes a module-private one, which the standalone comparator\nchallenges (`comparator/`) could not reproduce. -/\nnoncomputable def linearGaussianEnv (𝒳 : Set E) (θ : E) : Environment Unit 𝒳 ℝ :=\n  @stationaryEnv _ _ _ _ (linearGaussianKernel 𝒳 θ)\n    ⟨fun _ ↦ inferInstanceAs (IsProbabilityMeasure (gaussianReal _ 1))⟩","proof":"","source":{"path":"Maiti2026Power/LeanMachineLearning/LinearBandit.lean","start":59,"end":68,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/colt-2026-83/blob/3f6c0f296a3b7e4aa8fe333225505f5b2f61f9e0/Maiti2026Power/LeanMachineLearning/LinearBandit.lean#L59-L68"},"deps":[100],"outside":[],"external":[["Inner.inner","mathlib","definition"],["InnerProductSpace","mathlib","class"],["InnerProductSpace.toInner","mathlib","instance"],["Learning.Environment","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.stationaryEnv","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["MeasurableSpace","mathlib","class"],["Membership.mem","lean4","definition"],["NNReal","mathlib","definition"],["NNReal.instOne","mathlib","instance"],["NormedAddCommGroup","mathlib","class"],["NormedAddCommGroup.toSeminormedAddCommGroup","mathlib","instance"],["OfNat.ofNat","lean4","definition"],["One.toOfNat1","lean4","instance"],["OpensMeasurableSpace","mathlib","class"],["PUnit.instMeasurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["ProbabilityTheory.Kernel","mathlib","structure"],["ProbabilityTheory.Kernel.mk","mathlib","constructor"],["ProbabilityTheory.gaussianReal","mathlib","definition"],["PseudoMetricSpace.toUniformSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Real","mathlib","structure"],["Real.instRCLike","mathlib","instance"],["Real.measurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["SeminormedAddCommGroup.toPseudoMetricSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Set","mathlib","definition"],["Set.Elem","mathlib","definition"],["Set.instMembership","mathlib","instance"],["Subtype.instMeasurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Subtype.val","lean4","definition"],["UniformSpace.